From 822c87761f8587395b3e1a04b5386b2611252cd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nix-config downstream <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] pull_requests: add native stacked PR tools

Downstream implementation for github/github-mcp-server#2905.

The earlier upstream PR #2908 was rejected by API review because it used an
obsolete go-github request signature, pull_numbers/base request fields, and
undocumented PATCH/DELETE routes and response fields. This replacement follows
the review at https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pull/2908#issuecomment-5412937160
and the GitHub Stacked Pull Requests REST API documentation for version
2026-03-10:
https://docs.github.com/en/rest/pulls/stacks?apiVersion=2026-03-10

The downstream handlers preserve v1.11.0 scope and IFC conventions, including
repository-visibility metadata labels on successful stack responses.

Backport-base: github/github-mcp-server v1.11.0
Removal-condition: Remove this patch when a released github-mcp-server exposes
pull_request_stack_read and pull_request_stack_write with the documented
2026-03-10 list/get/create/add/unstack API contract.

---
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1230,6 +1230,24 @@
   - `repo`: Repository name (string, required)
   - `threadId`: The node ID of the review thread (e.g., PRRT_kwDOxxx). Required for resolve_thread and unresolve_thread methods. Get thread IDs from pull_request_read with method get_review_comments. (string, optional)
 
+- **pull_request_stack_read** - Read pull request stacks
+  - **OAuth Challenge Scopes**: `repo`
+  - `method`: Stack read operation: list stacks in a repository, or get one stack by stackNumber. (string, required)
+  - `owner`: Repository owner (string, required)
+  - `page`: Page number for list pagination (min 1). (number, optional)
+  - `perPage`: Results per page for list pagination (min 1, max 100). (number, optional)
+  - `pullNumber`: Filter list results to the stack containing this pull request. (number, optional)
+  - `repo`: Repository name (string, required)
+  - `stackNumber`: Stack number. Required for get. (number, optional)
+
+- **pull_request_stack_write** - Manage pull request stacks
+  - **OAuth Challenge Scopes**: `repo`
+  - `method`: Stack write operation: create, add pull requests to the top, or unstack eligible pull requests. (string, required)
+  - `owner`: Repository owner (string, required)
+  - `pullNumbers`: Pull request numbers ordered from the bottom of the new segment to the top. Create requires at least two; add requires at least one. (number[], optional)
+  - `repo`: Repository name (string, required)
+  - `stackNumber`: Stack number. Required for add and unstack. (number, optional)
+
 - **search_pull_requests** - Search pull requests
   - **OAuth Challenge Scopes**: `repo`
   - `fields`: Subset of fields to return for each pull request result. If omitted, all fields are returned. Use this to reduce response size when you only need specific fields; omitting 'body', 'reactions', and 'labels' in particular drops the largest per-result data. (string[], optional)
